--- ISSUE 8/10 ---
id: SEM-001
severity: moderate
category: semantics
found_by: static
related: OPR-023 (cite the same line — one edit may resolve all)
title: Use exactly one h1 per page
problem: 3 document(s) with more than one <h1> — there should be exactly one top-level heading per page.
why_it_matters: Multiple h1s erode the document outline that screen readers and search engines rely on; a single h1 anchors the page topic.
standards: wcag:1.3.1
locations:
  - makercentral_v1/commander v1.2.html:766:29 ~1599
     763|                                 ${task.status === 'completed' ? ICONS.completed : ICONS.inProgress}
     764|                                 <span class="status-pill ${getStatusStyles(task.status)} px-6 py-2.5">MCC-PROT-${task.id}</span>
     765|                             </div>
     766|                             <h1 class="text-8xl font-black heading-font text-slate-900 tracking-tighter mb-8">${task.feature}</h1> <<<
     767|                             <p class="text-3xl text-slate-500 font-medium leading-relaxed max-w-5xl">${task.description}</p>
     768|                         </header>
     769| 
  - makercentral_v1/commander-v-1.html:339:29 ~be9b
     336|                         </div>
     337|                         <div>
     338|                             <span class="status-pill status-${t.status} mb-2 inline-block">SYSTEM: ${t.status}</span>
     339|                             <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold heading-font tracking-tight">Mission Briefing</h1> <<<
     340|                         </div>
     341|                     </div>
     342| 
  - makercentral_v1/commander.html:766:29 ~1599
     763|                                 ${task.status === 'completed' ? ICONS.completed : ICONS.inProgress}
     764|                                 <span class="status-pill ${getStatusStyles(task.status)} px-6 py-2.5">MCC-PROT-${task.id}</span>
     765|                             </div>
     766|                             <h1 class="text-8xl font-black heading-font text-slate-900 tracking-tighter mb-8">${task.feature}</h1> <<<
     767|                             <p class="text-3xl text-slate-500 font-medium leading-relaxed max-w-5xl">${task.description}</p>
     768|                         </header>
     769| 
fix: Keep a single <h1> and structure the rest with <h2>–<h6> in order.

--- ISSUE 9/10 ---
id: SEM-004
severity: moderate
category: semantics
found_by: static
related: OPR-023 (cite the same line — one edit may resolve all)
title: Heading levels nest without skipping
problem: 7 heading level skip(s) (e.g. h2 → h4) — the document outline breaks for screen-reader heading navigation.
why_it_matters: Skipping from h2 to h4 breaks the implicit document tree; screen-reader users navigating by heading lose orientation.
standards: wcag:1.3.1, html:H42
